/target
Cargo.lock
*.bak

# ...except for the crates CI builds on their own. A lockfile that cannot be
# committed is one CI resolves fresh on every run, which is the one crate in the
# matrix whose dependency graph is not recorded anywhere - and `just check-locks`
# cannot notice, because there is no tracked lock to compare. `sdk/Cargo.lock`
# was already tracked in spite of this rule; i18n was not.
!/Cargo.lock
!/i18n/Cargo.lock
!/ui-kit/src-tauri/Cargo.lock

# TypeScript SDK packages (module-sdk, tauri-plugin-menu, tauri-plugin-shell)
node_modules/
package-lock.json
# Same exception: module-sdk and ui-kit are their own entries in the frontend
# matrix, and CI's `npm ci || npm install` silently falls back to an unpinned
# install when the lock is missing, so a dependency bump never reaches them.
!/module-sdk/package-lock.json
!/ui-kit/package-lock.json
!/tauri-plugin-menu/package-lock.json
dist/
*.tgz
